            "notes": "**Strategy**: Build is now online. Ramp your attack speed and find opportunity to kill while playing safe. Your choices depend on how well you can bully tank.\n\n**Upgrades**:\nThe idea now is to upgrade blues to purples that fulfill the same purpose. Start considering armor if you think you might be burst down or are constantly being challenged.\n\nAttack speed path:\n [Aftermarket Firing Pin](item_2485b212-b286-42d0-a2bd-20eb4396b054)  &rarr [Swift-Loader](item_eea704c1-7326-4298-9aa0-0f6491515f55) \n\nWeapon power path:\n [Shieldbuster](item_9ee1f150-537d-40b9-b975-7820fb1c6a66) /  [Talon Modification Module](item_c0ca1795-a3ea-4dc9-ae17-f34122574b3a) &rarr  [Codebreaker](item_caa96c7e-655f-4d03-9bd9-0f41937fec27) \n\nDefensive:\n [Shieldbuster](item_9ee1f150-537d-40b9-b975-7820fb1c6a66) /  [Talon Modification Module](item_c0ca1795-a3ea-4dc9-ae17-f34122574b3a) &rarr   [Weapon Jammer](item_72386db6-753e-413d-aa2a-f1389842f47f) \n\nTech choice:\n[Aerial Distresser](item_0fcb9020-c729-49b9-b398-3223797b6204) is your tech option versus Juno and Freja. It requires you to aim and you may not get kills reliably (don't go all-in). But applying pressure will help your team greatly and allow them not to snowball.",
